From 9f792ee1489b40a6bca789b1a1a397caad439bbb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 10:41:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] editor: start without arguments (double click) sets itself
 up, no launcher script

EdBootstrap (moho/editor, FAF_STUDIO_EDITOR builds only) runs first in WinMain. For an editor
exe (init_editor.lua next to it, or /editor) it makes the process DPI aware; started without
/init it also finds the FAForever data (FAF_DATA or %ProgramData%\FAForever), copies init_faf.lua,
SupComDataPath.lua and fa_path.lua, links cache / gamedata / movies / sounds / themes (junction,
else directory symlink), creates the user and working folders, sets the working folder to bin\,
sets FAFSTUDIO_UISCALE from the display scale for the first-run UI scale and adds the arguments
an editor start needs (/init init_editor.lua /editor /nomovie /nosound /windowed w h /log /eduser)
unless they are given. When it cannot go on it shows a message box (FAFSTUDIO_NOGUI: writes
logs\boot_message.txt) and ends with an exit code instead of crashing in the engine's start-up.
tests/EdBootstrapTest.cpp builds the module on its own (mingw / Wine / MSVC).

